Need `FrameCodec.isPing` exists. Use it. Update test 1:
```java
void connectsAndSendsPingThenEnvironmentAndResyncAfterPong() {
    start();
    assertEquals(1, transport.sent.size());
    assertTrue(FrameCodec.isPing(transport.sent.get(0)));
    transport.deliver(FrameCodec.encodePong());
    assertEquals(3, transport.sent.size());
    assertTrue(FrameCodec.isEnvironment(transport.sent.get(1)));
    assertTrue(FrameCodec.isResync(transport.sent.get(2)));
    ...
}
```
But the `start()` calls `session.start()`, which connects; `Listener.onOpen` sends PING and schedules a retry at 50ms. The test's assertion immediately after start should see 1 message. The scheduler might fire after 50ms, but the test is fast. Good.
- `transport.deliver(FrameCodec.encodePong())` triggers `onPong`, sends ENV+RESYNC, schedules a retry. `transport.sent` size 3. Good.

Test 2:
```java
void awaitSnapshotRetriesWhenTheInitialResyncIsLost() throws Exception {
    start();
    transport.deliver(FrameCodec.encodePong()); // ready
    transport.sent.clear(); // lose the first RESYNC
    Thread responder = ... if any RESYNC -> deliver snapshot ...
    ProtocolFrame snapshot = session.awaitSnapshot(3000);
    ...
    assertTrue(transport.sent.stream().anyMatch(FrameCodec::isResync));
}
```
- After PONG, `onPong` sends ENV+RESYNC and schedules retry at 50ms. We clear sent. The responder watches for a RESYNC. The scheduler's first retry after 50ms sends RESYNC; responder delivers snapshot. `awaitSnapshot` returns. Good.
- But `transport.sent.clear()` also removes ENV/RESYNC; the scheduler retry will add a RESYNC. Good.

Add test:
```java
@Test
void retriesPingUntilTheOriginIsReady() throws Exception {
    start();
    assertEquals(1, transport.sent.size());
    assertTrue(FrameCodec.isPing(transport.sent.get(0)));
    // Wait for the retry (50ms initial).
    long deadline = System.nanoTime() + 1_000_000_000L;
    while (transport.sent.stream().filter(FrameCodec::isPing).count() < 2 && System.nanoTime() < deadline) {
        Thread.sleep(5);
    }
    assertTrue(transport.sent.stream().filter(FrameCodec::isPing).count() >= 2);
    transport.deliver(FrameCodec.encodePong());
    assertTrue(transport.sent.stream().anyMatch(FrameCodec::isEnvironment));
    assertTrue(transport.sent.stream().anyMatch(FrameCodec::isResync));
}
```
- The scheduler's first PING retry at 50ms; wait up to 1s. Good.
- After PONG, ENV/RESYNC. The scheduled PING retry may still be pending; `onPong` cancels it. Good.

